[Music]  hey guys pete here today i'm going to  give you my spoiler-free impressions of  the expanse season 6. i don't usually do  videos like this and i don't normally  watch too far ahead when i have  screeners for a show but i started this  and even with taking notes and reading  the ninth book leviathan falls i still  ended up getting through it in a few  days and they did send out all six  episodes so here we are and there's a  lot of good to talk about here and i can  do that in a pretty spoiler-free way i'm  definitely not going to spoil any major  plot points so unless you just don't  want to know anything you should be able  to watch this video and with that out of  the way let's get into it  i suppose the main question you have if  you're here is is it a good ending and i  think the answer to that is yes given  the situation that this is the last  season that amazon prime video is making  i think it does a solid job of wrapping  up the story where it is and it leaves  things open for a future adaptation  there's still three more books to go my  quick spoiler-free review of leviathan  falls is they did stick the landing and  i hope that we'll one day be able to see  it but there's a lot to like in this  sixth season of the show there are some  really memorable character moments i  won't get into any specifics but holden  naomi and amos all had at least one  scene that hit harder than it had a  right to some of the changes they made  to the story helped to set some of these  up which means they're not necessarily  things that people who read the books  are waiting for which is a nice bonus  drummer has a scene that probably takes  the cake in this category for me but  whoever your favorite character is they  probably have a spotlight moment it does  feel like a final season in that regard  there are some really good callbacks and  some characters from prior seasons  popped back up there was at least one  that was kind of obscure and put a smile  on my face because i wasn't expecting it  that happens in the premiere and i think  you'll know the character from season 1  i'm talking about when you see it not to  create unrealistic expectations here  though there are definitely some that  are missing and are missed as far as how  the book played out there are a handful  of point of view characters from the  book that aren't even mentioned or  hinted at on the show another plus is  that there is a lot of high quality  space porn and not just battles but  there are those too but there's just a  lot of stuff that really looks authentic  here and they spend a lot of time in the  rasanante and it feels like we see more  of that than we ever did in the past  there's one scene in the premiere where  amos goes outside for some maintenance  and it's just leagues ahead of anything  they did in those first few seasons it's  not flashy or impressive other than it  just looks like wes chatham is actually  in a spacesuit in space walking on the  outside of a spaceship to do a job and  it's the way that they track him and how  it's set up perfectly it just allows  them to flex their muscles and show how  good they've gotten all of this over the  years there's another thing later in the  season where with a lesser show you  might think oh now you're just showing  off but the whole thing makes sense and  it's a cool sequence that feels like it  was spawned from writers who know what  their vfx crew is capable of the visual  effects also have pretty consistently  improved season after season and there  are some real set pieces here to look  forward to as i said the crew are in the  rossi for most of the season and there  are some battles going on which they  always do pretty well but i don't think  it's as wall to wall as some fans might  have been hoping i think realistically  it's on par with about how much we saw  in season five except there is one  really big and crazy season defining  sequence which didn't really disappoint  book readers will likely know what i'm  referring to here and it doesn't play  out exactly the same but they managed to  add a little more intensity with some of  the changes they made and overall most  of the changes in the season worked that  way but they also did cut out a lot  which makes me wonder how easy it will  be to follow for non-book readers and  that brings up some of the criticisms i  have it is super short there's just no  getting around it it's mostly paced well  as in it's in good hands as far as  streamlining things without dropping  important character stuff but it's still  less than 5 hours total and it goes by  fast with 45 minute episodes plus i'd  love that they added strange dogs and i  think it works well alongside with  what's happening in seoul but that takes  up a handful of minutes in a cold open  in every single episode another thing is  that you can tell this season is  different because of kovid it's subtle  but you can tell that they were  restricted in some ways i can't say for  sure but it seems possible that this has  something to do with which characters  they brought back and which ones they  didn't there are at least a few  characters who i expected to be involved  that are barely mentioned if at all it  just feels like they couldn't get them  back under these conditions and there  are some brand new characters which is  where i think the shortness really makes  a difference the casting and the  performances are good but if you're not  really paying attention to the dialogue  you might find yourself later thinking  like why is this person here there's  just not enough time to develop them and  there are other decisions they made that  seem to be a result of some combination  of these two things so there are some  issues i should mention that the  showrunner said at the new york city  comic con that there would be additional  shorts in the x-ray extras between each  episode i haven't seen those and they  could fill in some of the details that  feel light in these episodes apparently  there's going to be many episodes  between the episodes there was one  sequence that i was really looking  forward to seeing from the books that i  didn't think translated that well to the  show it was still good but i didn't  think it had the same tension and i'm  not sure it would come off as impressive  if you hadn't read the books but they  did add some interesting stuff i was  caught by surprise at a couple of points  and they definitely played around with  the idea that they could kill someone  off i won't confirm if they did or not  but there was at least one time when i  was yelling at the screen because i was  convinced it was a setup to end the  character overall i think they made it  work there's a nice balance between the  big stuff that's going on in space and  the intimate moments that happen on the  ship in between the characters and in  some ways it doesn't feel like the  ending we want as far as we know there's  more there but they made the end that we  get count and i think that's a good  place to leave things i'm gonna be  breaking down every episode as they come  out so i really don't need to say much  more here it's fast but it's not game of  thrones season eight i can guarantee  that to be fair though it does have a  much shorter run time than that i've  seen some things that i always wanted to  see on screen and i'm pretty happy about  it so let me know what you're hoping to  see and how you think things are gonna  play out please like this video if you  enjoyed it please subscribe to my  channel if you haven't already make sure  you check out my series recap for  everything you need to remember for  season six and thanks for watching i'll  talk to you soon

